ss='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-6" href="#5_Best_Storage_Practices_Ideal_Product_Forms" >5. Best Storage Practices &amp; Ideal Product Forms</a><ul class='ez-toc-list-level-3' ><li class='ez-toc-heading-level-3'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-7" href="#_Storage_Tips" > Storage Tips:</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-3'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-8" href="#Product_Types_Better_for_Long-Term_Storage" >Product Types Better for Long-Term Storage:</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-3'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-9" href="#Bulk_Purchasing_Tip" >Bulk Purchasing Tip:</a></li></ul></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-10" href="#6_FAQs" >6. FAQs:</a><ul class='ez-toc-list-level-3' ><li class='ez-toc-heading-level-3'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-11" href="#Does_milk_thistle_expire" >Does milk thistle expire?</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-3'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-12" href="#Do_milk_thistle_supplements_go_bad" >Do milk thistle supplements go bad?</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-3'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-13" href="#How_long_does_milk_thistle_last" >How long does milk thistle last?</a></li></ul></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-14" href="#7_Conclusion_What_Buyers_Need_to_Know" >7. Conclusion: What Buyers Need to Know</a><ul class='ez-toc-list-level-3' ><li class='ez-toc-heading-level-3'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-15" href="#Explore_Bulk_Milk_Thistle_Products_%E2%86%92" >Explore Bulk Milk Thistle Products →</a></li></ul></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class="ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-16" href="#References" >References</a></li></ul></nav></div><h2 data-start="963" data-end="990"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="1_What_Is_Milk_Thistle"></span>1. What Is Milk Thistle?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p data-start="992" data-end="1232">Milk thistle is a flowering plant native to the Mediterranean region and commonly used as an herbal supplement. Its seeds contain <strong data-start="1122" data-end="1135">silymarin</strong>, a group of flavonolignans with antioxidant, anti-inflammatory, and hepatoprotective properties.</p><p data-start="1234" data-end="1350">Milk thistle has been used in traditional medicine for over 2,000 years, mainly for liver and gallbladder disorders.</p><hr data-start="1352" data-end="1355" /><h2 data-start="1357" data-end="1397"><img src="/images/Does-Milk-Thistle-Expire-300x300.jpg" decoding="async" class="wp-image-1140 aligncenter" alt="Does Milk Thistle Expire" width="565" height="565" title="Does Milk Thistle Expire? How Long Does Milk Thistle Last &amp; How to Store It Right 4" /></h2><h2 data-start="1357" data-end="1397"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="2_What_Part_of_Milk_Thistle_Is_Used"></span>2. What Part of Milk Thistle Is Used?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p data-start="1399" data-end="1580">The <strong data-start="1403" data-end="1434">seeds (also called achenes)</strong> of milk thistle are the primary part used for medicinal purposes. Sometimes, the whole fruit or crushed seed powder is used in teas and capsules.</p><h3 data-start="1582" data-end="1599"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Common_forms"></span>Common forms:<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><ul data-start="1600" data-end="1727"><li data-start="1600" data-end="1632"><p data-start="1602" data-end="1632">Whole milk thistle seeds (raw)</p></li><li data-start="1633" data-end="1653"><p data-start="1635" data-end="1653">Ground seed powder</p></li><li data-start="1654" data-end="1695"><p data-start="1656" data-end="1695">Silymarin extract (standardized 70–80%)</p></li><li data-start="1696" data-end="1727"><p data-start="1698" data-end="1727">Oil (cold-pressed from seeds)</p></li></ul><hr data-start="1729" data-end="1732" /><h2 data-start="1734" data-end="1782"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="3_Nutritional_Analysis_of_Milk_Thistle_Parts"></span>3. Nutritional Analysis of Milk Thistle Parts<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><div class="_tableContainer_16hzy_1"><div class="_tableWrapper_16hzy_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse" tabindex="-1"><table class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" data-start="1784" data-end="2460"><thead data-start="1784" data-end="1895"><tr data-start="1784" data-end="1895"><th data-start="1784" data-end="1809" data-col-size="sm">Component</th><th data-start="1809" data-end="1833" data-col-size="sm">Whole Seed (per 100g)</th><th data-start="1833" data-end="1849" data-col-size="sm">Ground Powder</th><th data-start="1849" data-end="1875" data-col-size="sm">Silymarin Extract (80%)</th><th data-start="1875" data-end="1895" data-col-size="sm">Cold-Pressed Oil</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="2009" data-end="2460"><tr data-start="2009" data-end="2121"><td data-start="2009" data-end="2034" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2011" data-end="2024">Silymarin</strong></td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2034" data-end="2058">4–6%</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2058" data-end="2074">4–6%</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2074" data-end="2101">70–80%</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2101" data-end="2121">Trace</td></tr><tr data-start="2122" data-end="2234"><td data-start="2122" data-end="2147" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2124" data-end="2145">Fat (mostly PUFA)</strong></td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2147" data-end="2171">25–30g</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2171" data-end="2187">25–30g</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2187" data-end="2214">&lt;1g</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2214" data-end="2234">~98g</td></tr><tr data-start="2235" data-end="2347"><td data-start="2235" data-end="2260" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2237" data-end="2248">Protein</strong></td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2260" data-end="2284">18–20g</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2284" data-end="2300">18–20g</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2300" data-end="2327">&lt;1g</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2327" data-end="2347">0g</td></tr><tr data-start="2348" data-end="2460"><td data-start="2348" data-end="2373" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2350" data-end="2373">Shelf Life Estimate</strong></td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2373" data-end="2397">1–2 years</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2397" data-end="2413">12–18 months</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2413" data-end="2440">2–3 years</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="2440" data-end="2460">6–12 months</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"></div></div></div></div><p data-start="2462" data-end="2475"><strong data-start="2462" data-end="2473">Source:</strong></p><ul data-start="2476" data-end="2630"><li data-start="2476" data-end="2517"><p data-start="2478" data-end="2517">European Medicines Agency (EMA, 2018)</p></li><li data-start="2518" data-end="2568"><p data-start="2520" data-end="2568">U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) Database</p></li><li data-start="2569" data-end="2630"><p data-start="2571" data-end="2630">National Institutes of Health (NIH) Herbal Supplement Facts</p></li></ul><hr data-start="2632" data-end="2635" /><h2 data-start="2637" data-end="2683"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="4_What_Happens_When_Milk_Thistle_Goes_Bad"></span>4. What Happens When Milk Thistle Goes Bad?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p data-start="2685" data-end="2781">When expired or improperly stored, milk thistle may lose potency or develop harmful by-products:</p><ul data-start="2783" data-end="3158"><li data-start="2783" data-end="2895"><p data-start="2785" data-end="2895"><strong data-start="2785" data-end="2810">Silymarin degradation</strong>: Reduced antioxidant activity (source: Journal of Pharmacy and Pharmacology, 2014)</p></li><li data-start="2896" data-end="2999"><p data-start="2898" data-end="2999"><strong data-start="2898" data-end="2913">Rancid oils</strong>: Cold-pressed oil oxidizes, forming <strong data-start="2950" data-end="2975">aldehydes and ketones</strong>, which are cytotoxic.</p></li><li data-start="3000" data-end="3158"><p data-start="3002" data-end="3158"><strong data-start="3002" data-end="3020">Mycotoxin risk</strong>: Moisture exposure may lead to mold growth, especially <strong data-start="3076" data-end="3098">Aspergillus flavus</strong>, which can produce <strong data-start="3118" data-end="3132">aflatoxins</strong>, known liver carcinogens.</p></li></ul><blockquote data-start="3160" data-end="3340"><p data-start="3162" data-end="3340">💡 According to a 2021 study in <em data-start="3194" data-end="3208">Food Control</em>, improperly stored milk thistle seeds showed a 3.4% contamination rate with detectable aflatoxins in humid conditions above 65% RH.</p></blockquote><hr data-start="3342" data-end="3345" /><h2 data-start="3347" data-end="3397"><img src="/images/Does-Milk-Thistle-Expire-2-300x300.jpg" decoding="async" class="wp-image-1141 aligncenter" alt="Does Milk Thistle Expire" width="575" height="575" title="Does Milk Thistle Expire? How Long Does Milk Thistle Last &amp; How to Store It Right 5" /></h2><h2 data-start="3347" data-end="3397"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="5_Best_Storage_Practices_Ideal_Product_Forms"></span>5. Best Storage Practices &amp; Ideal Product Forms<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><h3 data-start="3399" data-end="3418"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="_Storage_Tips"></span> Storage Tips:<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><ul data-start="3419" data-end="3532"><li data-start="3419" data-end="3453"><p data-start="3421" data-end="3453">Store in <strong data-start="3430" data-end="3453">airtight containers</strong></p></li><li data-start="3454" data-end="3500"><p data-start="3456" data-end="3500">Keep in a <strong data-start="3466" data-end="3500">cool, dry place (&lt;25°C / 77°F)</strong></p></li><li data-start="3501" data-end="3532"><p data-start="3503" data-end="3532">Avoid <strong data-start="3509" data-end="3532">sunlight &amp; humidity</strong></p></li></ul><h3 data-start="3534" data-end="3584"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Product_Types_Better_for_Long-Term_Storage"></span>Product Types Better for Long-Term Storage:<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><div class="_tableContainer_16hzy_1"><div class="_tableWrapper_16hzy_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse" tabindex="-1"><table class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" data-start="3586" data-end="4135"><thead data-start="3586" data-end="3675"><tr data-start="3586" data-end="3675"><th data-start="3586" data-end="3608" data-col-size="sm">Product Type</th><th data-start="3608" data-end="3621" data-col-size="sm">Shelf Life</th><th data-start="3621" data-end="3647" data-col-size="sm">Best Packaging</th><th data-start="3647" data-end="3675" data-col-size="sm">Cost Efficiency for Bulk</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="3768" data-end="4135"><tr data-start="3768" data-end="3859"><td data-start="3768" data-end="3790" data-col-size="sm">Whole Seed</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="3790" data-end="3803">18–24 mo</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="3803" data-end="3830">Vacuum-sealed PE bags</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="3830" data-end="3859">★★★★★</td></tr><tr data-start="3860" data-end="3951"><td data-start="3860" data-end="3882" data-col-size="sm">Silymarin Extract</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="3882" data-end="3895">24–36 mo</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="3895" data-end="3922">Aluminum foil pouches</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="3922" data-end="3951">★★★★☆</td></tr><tr data-start="3952" data-end="4043"><td data-start="3952" data-end="3974" data-col-size="sm">Ground Powder</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="3974" data-end="3987">12–18 mo</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="3987" data-end="4014">Airtight HDPE containers</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="4014" data-end="4043">★★★☆☆</td></tr><tr data-start="4044" data-end="4135"><td data-start="4044" data-end="4066" data-col-size="sm">Cold-Pressed Oil</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="4066" data-end="4079">6–12 mo</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="4079" data-end="4106">Amber glass bottles</td><td data-col-size="sm" data-start="4106" data-end="4135">★★☆☆☆</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"></div></div></div></div><h3 data-start="4137" data-end="4161"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Bulk_Purchasing_Tip"></span>Bulk Purchasing Tip:<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><blockquote data-start="4162" data-end="4323"><p data-start="4164" data-end="4323">Choose <strong data-start="4171" data-end="4186">whole seeds</strong> or <strong data-start="4190" data-end="4225">standardized silymarin extracts</strong> with <strong data-start="4231" data-end="4238">COA</strong> and <strong data-start="4243" data-end="4259">moisture &lt;8%</strong>, vacuum-sealed in aluminum or PE inner bags with outer cartons.</p></blockquote><hr data-start="4325" data-end="4328" /><h2 data-start="4330" data-end="4373"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="6_FAQs"></span>6. FAQs:<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><h3 data-start="4375" data-end="4408"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Does_milk_thistle_expire"></span><strong data-start="4379" data-end="4408">Does milk thistle expire?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><p data-start="4409" data-end="4544">Yes, milk thistle expires like all natural products. Depending on form and storage, its shelf life ranges from <strong data-start="4520" data-end="4543">6 months to 3 years</strong>.</p><h3 data-start="4546" data-end="4589"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Do_milk_thistle_supplements_go_bad"></span><strong data-start="4550" data-end="4589">Do milk thistle supplements go bad?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><p data-start="4590" data-end="4754">Yes. Expired milk thistle supplements may lose potency and could become rancid or contaminated with mold. Always check <strong data-start="4709" data-end="4725">expiry dates</strong> and <strong data-start="4730" data-end="4753">packaging integrity</strong>.</p><h3 data-start="4756" data-end="4796"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="How_long_does_milk_thistle_last"></span><strong data-start="4760" data-end="4796">How long does milk thistle last?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><ul data-start="4797" data-end="4903"><li data-start="4797" data-end="4828"><p data-start="4799" data-end="4828">Whole seed: up to 24 months</p></li><li data-start="4829" data-end="4857"><p data-start="4831" data-end="4857">Extract: up to 36 months</p></li><li data-start="4858" data-end="4882"><p data-start="4860" data-end="4882">Powder: 12–18 months</p></li><li data-start="4883" data-end="4903"><p data-start="4885" data-end="4903">Oil: 6–12 months</p></li></ul><hr data-start="4905" data-end="4908" /><h2 data-start="4910" data-end="4952"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="7_Conclusion_What_Buyers_Need_to_Know"></span>7. Conclusion: What Buyers Need to Know<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p data-start="4954" data-end="5258">Based on verified data and research from the EMA, USDA, and peer-reviewed journals, <strong data-start="5038" data-end="5118">milk thistle’s shelf life depends heavily on its form and storage conditions</strong>. Bulk buyers looking for maximum shelf life and quality assurance should prioritize <strong data-start="5203" data-end="5257">standardized extracts or vacuum-packed whole seeds</strong>.</p><p data-st